{"availability":"available","full":"danielsaed/F1-steering-angle-model","name":"F1-steering-angle-model","description":"Computer Vision model that predicts steering angles from F1 onboard camera footage.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":21,"forks":1,"created":"2025-03-04T04:55:39Z","updated":"2025-11-19T08:36:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://daniel-saed-f1-steering-angle-model.hf.space/","topics":["cnn-model","computer-vision","f1","machie-learning","machinelearning","streamlit","yolov8"],"demo":"https://daniel-saed-f1-steering-angle-model.hf.space/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:05.333Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:05.333Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T09:07:05.333Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T09:07:05.333Z","stars":21,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A machine learning application that predicts steering angles from F1 onboard camera footage.","Steering input is one of the key fundamental insights into driving behavior, performance and style. However, there is no straightforward public source, tool or API to access steering angle data. The only available source is onboard camera footage, which comes with its own limitations, such as camera position, shadows, weather conditions, and lighting."],"features":["The F1 Steering Angle Prediction Model uses a CNN based on EfficientNet-B0 to predict steering angles from a F1 onboard camera footage, trained with over 25,000 images (7000 manual labaled augmented to 25000) and…","Currentlly the model is able to predict steering angles from 180° to -180° with a 3°-5° of error on ideal contitions.","EfficientNet-B0 and YOLOv8-seg nano are exported to ONNX format, and images are resized to 224x224 allowing it to run on low-end devices."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/danielsaed/F1-steering-angle-model/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"be0eaa024a1cc93093001f61ce6e5fc951589196dae7